findings.body:
The helper `getDisplayEmail` uses `/\+[a-zA-Z0-9]{25}/`, which has no end anchor and no lookahead for `@`. Any `+` followed by 25 or more alphanumerics gets truncated, not only CUID suffixes. The regex also does not check that the `+tag` sits directly before the `@`.

I ran the regex. `a+bcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz1@x.com` becomes `a1@x.com`, which drops the 25-character tag and leaves a stray character behind. The same regex is also applied to `displayGuests` and `reassignedTo`, so the corruption spreads.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="96-98"}

Tighten the match to the CUID position just before `@`, and treat the helper as the single source of truth for both call sites.

::suggestion{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="96-98"}
private getDisplayEmail(email: string): string {
  return email.replace(/\+[a-z0-9]{25}(?=@)/, "");
}

In `getOutputRecurringSeatedBookings` the PR replaces `return transformed.sort(...)` with `return transformed;`. The PR description says nothing about this, and no test covers it. The method is called from `BookingsService` for recurring seated bookings, and the sort was ordering results by `start`.

The result now follows `bookingsIds` order. That order comes from `getRecurringByUidWithAttendeesAndUserAndEvent`, which may not sort by start time. The fix is to restore the original sort, or to include the change in its own PR with a test.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="411-425"}

Some seated-booking assertions compare the output with itself, so they check nothing about the new field. In `seated-bookings.e2e-spec.ts`, line 280 expects `displayEmail: createdSeatedBooking.attendees[0].displayEmail`, and line 424 expects `displayEmail: attendee?.displayEmail`. Those values come from the response under test. Because `toEqual` treats `undefined` as a match for missing keys, the assertion passes even if the field is absent.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/controllers/e2e/seated-bookings.e2e-spec.ts" lines="277-282"}

Assert against the literal expected email, as the other tests in this PR do.
